<!--
Native ARM64 build of DriverManager, sharing DriverManager.cpp with DriverManager.vcxproj by
relative-path reference (not a copy). This exists solely because SetupInstallServicesFromInfSectionW
(service registration, called from InstallDriver in DriverManager.cpp) rejects calls from a process
running under x64 emulation on an ARM64 host, even though DiInstallDriverW (DriverStore staging)
succeeds fine under emulation there (verified on real hardware). The x64 build's wmain() detects a
native ARM64 host at startup and relays the entire invocation to this binary (DriverManager_arm64.exe,
shipped alongside it in the same install directory by KbdLayerSetup.wixproj's CMP_DriverTools
component) rather than branching inside InstallDriver/UninstallDriver themselves. When this binary
itself runs (already native ARM64), that relay branch is compiled out (#if !defined(_M_ARM64)) and
it just proceeds normally.

Produces DriverManager_arm64.exe (TargetName intentionally left at the project default, unlike the
kbdlayer_arm64.vcxproj kernel driver project: nothing parses this filename out of an .inf,
RelaunchViaArm64Companion in DriverManager.cpp hardcodes this exact name).
-->
